mcs51: add --fixed-regbank to skip PSW reset in ISR prologue

Every mcs51 ISR prologue emits 'mov psw,#0x00' to select register bank 0.
When the whole program uses only the default bank (no function declared
__using(1..3)), that store is redundant.  --fixed-regbank lets the user
assert this invariant so the store is dropped, saving 3 bytes and 2
cycles per interrupt.  The instruction is still emitted for any function
whose FUNC_REGBANK is non-zero.

	* src/SDCCglobl.h (struct options): New field fixedRegbank.
	* src/SDCCmain.c (optionsTable): New option --fixed-regbank.
	* src/SDCCerr.h (enum): New warning code W_FIXED_REGBANK_USING.
	* src/SDCCerr.c (messages): Message text for W_FIXED_REGBANK_USING.
	* src/mcs51/gen.c (genFunction): In the ISR prologue, skip the PSW
	bank-select store when options.fixedRegbank is set and the function
	uses bank 0.
	Also emit W_FIXED_REGBANK_USING when --fixed-regbank is combined
	with any function that uses a non-default register bank.

